<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Nepomuceno Almonte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1803–1869</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Nepomuceno Almonte was a Mexican soldier and diplomat, son of the independence leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-morelos">José María Morelos</a>. A conservative, he supported French intervention and headed the regency that governed in the name of the Second Mexican Empire from 1863 until Maximilian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> arrived in 1864. He then served as the emperor's grand marshal and died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-nepomuceno-almonte.jpg" alt="Juan Nepomuceno Almonte" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cruces y Campa, México, 2d de S. Francisco, no. 4 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_Nepomuceno_Almonte_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
